e_problemDescription__T4cPe"><p>You are given a sorted array that contains =
unique values, along with an integer target.</p><ul>
<li>If the array contains the target value, return its index.</li>
<li>Otherwise, <strong>return the insertion index</strong>. This is the ind=
ex where the target would be if it were inserted in order, maintaining the =
sorted sequence of the array.</li>
</ul><h4 id=3D"example-1">Example 1:</h4><pre><code class=3D"hljs language-=
python">Input: nums =3D [<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span class=
